{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_javascript_pages_phase_5_built_in_library_07_string_methods_01_slicing_and_splitting_page", "label": "Slicing and splitting", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/javascript/pages/phase-5-built-in-library/07-string-methods/01-slicing-and-splitting.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_javascript_pages_phase_5_built_in_library_07_string_methods_01_slicing_and_splitting_string_immutability", "label": "Strings are immutable", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/javascript/pages/phase-5-built-in-library/07-string-methods/01-slicing-and-splitting.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Every string method returns a new string, so no defensive copy is needed."}, {"id": "docs_javascript_pages_phase_5_built_in_library_07_string_methods_01_slicing_and_splitting_slice", "label": "String.prototype.slice", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/javascript/pages/phase-5-built-in-library/07-string-methods/01-slicing-and-splitting.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_javascript_pages_phase_5_built_in_library_07_string_methods_01_slicing_and_splitting_substring", "label": "String.prototype.substring", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/javascript/pages/phase-5-built-in-library/07-string-methods/01-slicing-and-splitting.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Treats negatives as 0 and swaps start > end, hiding bugs behind a plausible substring."}, {"id": "docs_javascript_pages_phase_5_built_in_library_07_string_methods_01_slicing_and_splitting_use_slice_not_substring", "label": "Use slice, not substring", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/javascript/pages/phase-5-built-in-library/07-string-methods/01-slicing-and-splitting.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "slice matches Array.prototype.slice, supports negative indices, and returns empty when start > end so mistakes surface."}, {"id": "docs_javascript_pages_phase_5_built_in_library_07_string_methods_01_slicing_and_splitting_at", "label": "String.prototype.at", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/javascript/pages/phase-5-built-in-library/07-string-methods/01-slicing-and-splitting.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Accepts negative indices; bracket notation does not. Out of range returns undefined, unlike charAt which returns empty string."}, {"id": "docs_javascript_pages_phase_5_built_in_library_07_string_methods_01_slicing_and_splitting_split", "label": "String.prototype.split", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/javascript/pages/phase-5-built-in-library/07-string-methods/01-slicing-and-splitting.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "No separator returns [whole string]. limit truncates and discards the remainder. Capture groups in a regex separator are included."}, {"id": "docs_javascript_pages_phase_5_built_in_library_07_string_methods_01_slicing_and_splitting_split_empty_csv", "label": "empty string split is [\"\"]", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/javascript/pages/phase-5-built-in-library/07-string-methods/01-slicing-and-splitting.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "\"\".split(\",\") is [\"\"] not [], so field counts are 1 for empty CSV input."}, {"id": "docs_javascript_pages_phase_5_built_in_library_07_string_methods_01_slicing_and_splitting_split_code_units", "label": "split(\"\") splits UTF-16 code units", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/javascript/pages/phase-5-built-in-library/07-string-methods/01-slicing-and-splitting.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Emoji and other non-BMP characters become surrogate halves. [...str] and Array.from yield code points."}, {"id": "docs_javascript_pages_phase_5_built_in_library_07_string_methods_01_slicing_and_splitting_intl_segmenter", "label": "Intl.Segmenter", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/javascript/pages/phase-5-built-in-library/07-string-methods/01-slicing-and-splitting.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Code points are not graphemes; skin-tone and family emoji are several code points that display as one character."}, {"id": "docs_javascript_pages_phase_5_built_in_library_07_string_methods_01_slicing_and_splitting_join", "label": "Array.prototype.join", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/javascript/pages/phase-5-built-in-library/07-string-methods/01-slicing-and-splitting.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "null and undefined become empty strings, so missing values silently become empty CSV fields."}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_javascript_pages_phase_5_built_in_library_07_string_methods_01_slicing_and_splitting_use_slice_not_substring", "target": "docs_javascript_pages_phase_5_built_in_library_07_string_methods_01_slicing_and_splitting_slice", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/javascript/pages/phase-5-built-in-library/07-string-methods/01-slicing-and-splitting.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_javascript_pages_phase_5_built_in_library_07_string_methods_01_slicing_and_splitting_use_slice_not_substring", "target": "docs_javascript_pages_phase_5_built_in_library_07_string_methods_01_slicing_and_splitting_substring", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/javascript/pages/phase-5-built-in-library/07-string-methods/01-slicing-and-splitting.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_javascript_pages_phase_5_built_in_library_07_string_methods_01_slicing_and_splitting_slice", "target": "docs_javascript_pages_phase_5_built_in_library_07_string_methods_01_slicing_and_splitting_substring", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/javascript/pages/phase-5-built-in-library/07-string-methods/01-slicing-and-splitting.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_javascript_pages_phase_5_built_in_library_07_string_methods_01_slicing_and_splitting_split_empty_csv", "target": "docs_javascript_pages_phase_5_built_in_library_07_string_methods_01_slicing_and_splitting_split", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/javascript/pages/phase-5-built-in-library/07-string-methods/01-slicing-and-splitting.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_javascript_pages_phase_5_built_in_library_07_string_methods_01_slicing_and_splitting_split_code_units", "target": "docs_javascript_pages_phase_5_built_in_library_07_string_methods_01_slicing_and_splitting_split", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/javascript/pages/phase-5-built-in-library/07-string-methods/01-slicing-and-splitting.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_javascript_pages_phase_5_built_in_library_07_string_methods_01_slicing_and_splitting_intl_segmenter", "target": "docs_javascript_pages_phase_5_built_in_library_07_string_methods_01_slicing_and_splitting_split_code_units", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/javascript/pages/phase-5-built-in-library/07-string-methods/01-slicing-and-splitting.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_javascript_pages_phase_5_built_in_library_07_string_methods_01_slicing_and_splitting_join", "target": "docs_javascript_pages_phase_5_built_in_library_07_string_methods_01_slicing_and_splitting_split", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/javascript/pages/phase-5-built-in-library/07-string-methods/01-slicing-and-splitting.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_javascript_pages_phase_5_built_in_library_07_string_methods_01_slicing_and_splitting_page", "target": "docs_javascript_pages_phase_5_built_in_library_07_string_methods_02_trimming_padding_replacing_page", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/javascript/pages/phase-5-built-in-library/07-string-methods/01-slicing-and-splitting.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}], "hyperedges": []}